{"text": "Subtracting 299 days from 1842-11-29:  \n1842 is not a leap year.  \nDays in Nov (29 to 30) = 1, Dec = 31, Jan = 31, Feb = 28, Mar = 31, Apr = 30, May = 31, Jun = 30, Jul = 31, Aug = 31, Sep = 30, Oct = 31, Nov = 30, Dec = 31.  \nSum: 1+31=32, +31=63, +28=91, +31=122, +30=152, +31=183, +30=213, +31=244, +31=275, +30=305, +31=336, +30=366, +31=397 → too far.  \nWe need 299 days: 1+31+31+28+31+30+31+30+31+31+30+31 = 1+31=32, +31=63, +28=91, +31=122, +30=152, +31=183, +30=213, +31=244, +31=275, +30=305 → 305 days from Nov 29 goes into 1843-09-30. But we need to subtract 299, not add.  \nBetter: go back 299 days from 1842-11-29.  \n1842-11-29 back 29 days → 1842-10-31. Remaining 299-29=270 days.  \nGo back into 1841: 1842 is not leap, 1841 is not leap. Days in 1841 after Jan 1: from 1842-01-01 back 1 day → 1841-12-31. Count back from 1841-12-31:  \nDec 31 days = 31, Nov=30, Oct=31, Sep=30, Aug=31, Jul=31, Jun=30, May=31, Apr=30, Mar=31, Feb=28, Jan=31.  \nSum: 31+30=61, +31=92, +30=122, +31=153, +31=184, +30=214, +31=245, +30=275, +31=306, +28=334, +31=365 total days", "latency": 18.446481227874756, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 238, "completion_tokens": 512, "total_tokens": 750}, "error": null}